            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgeons are frequently confronted with a patient who has recently had a myocardial infarction, needs an operation urgently, or has a postoperative infarction. This paper examines the extreme caution necessary when surgery is scheduled for a patient with coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
